The Oflag IV-C prison camp was known to its prisoners as Colditz Castle, and to the surrounding community as Oflag IV-C. Notable features of the camp included its high security, with a large German garrison in the outer court (Kommandantur) and a 90 ft (27 m) tall building where prisoners lived, surrounded by barbed wire and watched by armed sentries.
