How did Albert Giacometti's unique style or contributions in his profession impact his fame and legacy?
Alberto Giacometti's unique style and contributions in his profession significantly impacted his fame and legacy. His distinctive approach to sculpture, which often featured elongated and abstracted human figures, was influenced by philosophical questions about the human condition and existential debates. This style, combined with his experimentation with artistic styles such as Cubism and Surrealism, set him apart from other artists of his time.

Giacometti's willingness to rework and destroy his models, often setting them aside for years, also added to his enigmatic and innovative reputation. The rarity of his prints, with some editions limited to only 30 copies, further contributed to his fame and legacy.

As a result, Giacometti's work was in high demand, and he became one of the most important sculptors of the 20th century. His exhibitions throughout Europe in his later years solidified his position as a leading artist of his time.
