Who were the key figures involved in the hostage crisis at the US Embassy in Tehran in 1979?
Based on the provided context, the key figures involved in the hostage crisis at the US Embassy in Tehran in 1979 were:

1. Ayatollah Mohammad Beheshti (set up the Office for Strengthening Unity, which played a central role in the seizure of the US Embassy)
2. Mahmoud Ahmadinejad (member of the OSU central council)
3. Ebrahim Asgharzadeh (member of the OSU central council)
4. Mohsen Kadivar (member of the OSU central council)
5. Mohsen Aghajari (member of the OSU central council)
6. Abbas Abdi (member of the OSU central council)
7. Ayatollah Ruhallah Khomeini (Iranian Supreme Ruler, Beheshti's superior)
8. Hector Villalon and Christian Bourget (represented Iranian Foreign Minister Sadegh Ghotbzadeh in initial negotiations)
9. Sadegh Ghotbzadeh (Iranian Foreign Minister)
10. Kenneth Kraus (US Marine taken hostage by the Organization of Iranian People's Fedai Guerrillas)
11. William Sullivan (US Ambassador to Iran, surrendered the embassy to save lives)
12. Ebrahim Yazdi (Iranian Foreign Minister, assisted in returning the embassy to US hands)
