Research the specific artificial heart transplant that is widely recognized as the first, including the date, location, and details of the procedure.
The first artificial heart transplant was performed by Dr. Robert Jarvik and Dr. Barney Clark, but it was not a traditional transplant. Instead, it was an implantation of a total artificial heart, known as the Jarvik-7. 

The procedure took place on December 2, 1982, at the University of Utah in Salt Lake City, Utah, USA. The recipient, Dr. Barney Clark, a 61-year-old dentist, lived for 112 days after the implantation.
