In Irish folklore, leprechauns are depicted as mischievous fairy creatures who spend their time making shoes and have a hidden pot of gold at the end of the rainbow. They are solitary creatures who are said to grant three wishes to humans who capture them. They are often associated with Irish mythology and are believed to be derived from the Tuatha Dé Danann.
