When were red and yellow cards first introduced in English football leagues, and what was the context surrounding their adoption?
Red and yellow cards were first introduced in domestic English football in the 1976-77 season. This was done to clarify referee decisions and make them clearer to both players and spectators, as a result of an incident in 1970 where a referee's decision was unclear. The idea was inspired by the principle of traffic lights, where yellow indicates caution and red indicates stop.
